  "raw_text": "70\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb57\n):\n \n(Wihta nani)\n \n(Jirimaya)\n \nalki liwanhta pakni drapapa ailal bri kan ba ra lulkan\n \n–\n \n(The leaders)\n \ncapturing (Jeremiah)\n\nthrew (him) in\n \na\n \ndeep well having a lot of mud\n \n/ (Los líderes) capturando\n \na\n \n(Jeremías) lo arrojaron a un pozo profundo con mucho\n\nlodo\n)\n\nDrapapa daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make muddy\n \n/ enlodar\n\nDrawaia\n \n(v) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nDrabaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto stretch, to extend\n \n/ extender, estirar\n\nDringbaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrihngbaia\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nDringwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto tear down, to knock down, to smash, to break\n \n/ derribar,\naplastar, romper\n\nDringwaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrihngwaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nDringbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be broken down, to be knocked down, to be smashed\n \n/\nestar descompuesto, ser derribado, ser aplastado\n\nDring\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrinh\n)\n \npruaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto faint from exhaustion, to pass out\n \n/ desmayarse por el agotamiento, desmayarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf28\n):\n \nPiu bani G\nȃ\nd ra kasak luki bas, dring prui baku damra walma sin\n \n–\n \nAlways be trusting in God, even when you feel\noverwhelmed\n \n/ Confíe siempre en Dios, incluso cuando se sienta abrumado)\n\nDring\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrinh\n)\n \nswapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get tired, to get weary, to become exhausted\n \n/ cansarse, agotarse\n\nDring\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrinh\n)\n \nswapras\n \n–\n \nnot tired, not weary, not exhausted\n \n/ no cansado, no agotado, sin cansancio\n\nDrop\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDrap\n\nDruga\n \n(not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndrugs\n \n/ drogas\n\nDruga yus munaia\n \n(\nfy,lv,bh\n,\nll,\n \nbut not in / pero no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto use drugs\n \n/ usar drogas\n\nDruga wakia bak dingkaia\n \n(\nfy25\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto put drugs in the body through the vein, to use drugs intravenously\n \n/\nponer drogas en el cuerpo a través de la vena, usar drogas por vía intravenosa\n\nDrusbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto peel, to skin, to strip (a tree of its fruit or a king of his crown), to shell, to thresh, to crush, to tear apart\n\n/ pelar, desollar, descascarar, despojar (un árbol de sus frutas o un rey de su corona),\n \ndesgranar, machacar,\n \ndespedazar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Isikiel 21:26\n):\n \nking kraunka ba drusbi\n \n–\n \nstripping away the king’s crown\n \n/ despojando a la corona del rey)\n\nDu\narsap\n \n(n/s) (\nUnu\n,\nUno\n-\nt\nc\n;\n \nPuntara\n,\nDuarsap\n-\nbc\n;\n \nDuarsap\n,\nPuno\n,\nPuntara\n-\ndict\n;\n \nPuno,Puntara\n-\ndictu\n;\n)\n \n–\n \nsoursop fruit,\n\nsoursop tree\n \n/ g\nuan\ná\nbana\n\n(Note/Nota: Creole/Criollo\n \n-\n \nsoursap)\n\nDubil\n \n–\n \ndouble\n \n/ doble\n\nDukia\n \n(\ndb,dbta,lrw,dict,dictu,bm,jl,fy,gf,ll,km\n;\n \nDukya\n-\nsln,bw,bh,lv,kt,sny\n)\n \n–\n \n(construct\n \nirregular\n \nfrom\n/de:\n \nDiara\n)\n \n–\n \nthe\n\nthing, the belonging, the article, the property,\n \nthe\n \naffair\n, the\n \nitem\n \n/ la cosa, la pertenencia, el artículo, la propiedad, el\n\nasunto\n\n(Construct other/otras:\n \nDuki\n \n–\n \nmy thing\n \n/ mi cosa;\n \nDukiam\n \n–\n \nyour thing\n \n/ tu cosa;\n \nAi dukia\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their thing\n \n/ su cosa)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nDîa muni yamni sa wan dukia nani yawan nit kabia ba asla dauki ridi briaia?\n \n–\n \nWhy is it good to have our\nthings that we will need all together and ready?; (Why is it important to have our emergency kit ready?) /\n \n¿Por qué es bueno que\ntengamos las cosas que necesitaremos juntas y listas?; (¿Por qué es importante tener nuestro kit de emergencia listo?)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nDiara yamni sa manis spirit dukia nani ba kulkisma\n \n–\n \nIt's good that you repect spiritual things\n \n/ Es bueno que respetes las\n\ncosas espirituales)\n\nDukia daukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nDukya daukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto serve, to do the will of\n \n/ servir, hacer la voluntad de\n\n(Construct:\n \nDuki daukaia\n \n–\n \nto serve me, to do my will\n \n/ servirme, hacer mi voluntad;\n \nDukiam daukaia\n \n–\n \nto serve you, to do\nyour will\n \n/ servirte, hacer tu voluntad)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nNawas piua ra yang dîa dukia kau pain daukaia sip sna ki, Armagedan balbia kat bara Jehova pri ai\nsâkbia?\n \n–\n \nAt the present time, what am I able to do to serve better until Armageddon comes and Jehovah frees me?\n \n/ En\nla actualidad, ¿qué puedo hacer para servir mejor hasta que llegue el Armagedón y Jehová me libere?)\n\nDukia dadaukra\n \n(a/t:\n \nDukya dadaukra\n-\nmy53\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nservant\n \n/ sirviente\n\n(Construct:\n \nDuki dadaukra\n \n–\n \nmy servant\n \n/ mi sirviente;\n \nDukiam dadaukra\n \n–\n \nyour servant\n \n/ tu sirviente)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 45:4\n):\n \nduki dadaukra Jekob\n \n–\n \nmy servant Jacob\n \n/ mi sirviente Jacob)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb31\n):\n \nWan mapara aiklabaia apia pramis munma kaka, dukiam dadaukra nani kamna\n \n–\n \nIf you promise\n\nthat you won’t fight against us, we will be your servants\n \n/ Si prometes que no pelearás contra nosotros, seremos\ntus sirvientes)\n\nTasba dukya nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nearth’s resources\n \n/ recursos de la tierra\n\nDukiara\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nD\nukyara\n)\n \n(pos)\n \n–\n \nabout\n, for, for the purpose of\n, for the purpose\n, in order to\n \n/ sobre,\n \nacerca de,\n \npara, con el\n\nfin de\n, po\nr\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-19\n):\n \nSip sa kaka, makabi walanka nani upla ra dauks witin dîa luki ba nu takaia dukiara.\n \n–\n \nIf possible, ask the person\nquestions in order to come to know what he/she is thinking.\n \n/ Si es posible, hágale preguntas a la persona para saber qué está\npensando.)",
